    "subTopics": [
      {
        "id": "sub-1",
        "title": "1. What is an Inversion FVG (iFVG)? When Support Inverts into Resistance",
        "content": "\n        <p class=\"mb-3\">Most retail traders lose money trying to buy every single FVG. When smart money wants to reverse the market, they intentionally crush through an existing FVG with aggressive volume.</p>\n        <p class=\"mb-3\">Once price closes completely through the FVG box, that box is labeled as an <strong>Inversion FVG (iFVG)</strong>. What was once expected support is now certified resistance.</p>\n      "
      },
      {
        "id": "sub-2",
        "title": "2. The 15-Bar Inversion Rule: Validating High-Velocity Institutional Breaks",
        "content": "\n        <p class=\"mb-3\">According to the DodgysDD quant specification, the FVG must be violently inverted within <strong>15 bars</strong> of its formation. Slow, drifting penetrations do not qualify; only high-velocity displacement candles count as institutional inversions.</p>\n      "
      },
      {
        "id": "sub-3",
        "title": "3. The 12-Bar Retest Window & Anti-Hunt ATR Stop Buffer",
        "content": "\n        <p class=\"mb-3\">Once inverted, price must retest the Grey Dashed iFVG Box within <strong>12 bars</strong>. To prevent retail stop hunts, position your stop loss beyond the iFVG box with an Anti-Hunt buffer of 0.40 &times; ATR.</p>\n      "
      }
    ],
    "tradeDetails": {
      "setupType": "DodgysDD Inversion FVG (iFVG) Retest Execution",
      "instrument": "NIFTY Spot / ATM Put (PE) Option",
      "entryTrigger": "Pullback retest into the Grey Dashed iFVG Box within the 12-bar window",
      "stopLoss": "1 tick beyond the opposite side of the iFVG box + 0.4x ATR buffer (-45 pts)",
      "target1": "First external swing low (+95 pts / 1:2.1 RR)",
      "target2": "Higher timeframe liquidity pool (+180 pts / 1:4.0 RR)",
      "riskReward": "1:4.0",
      "executionChecklist": [
        "Prior FVG is cleanly breached and closed beyond within 15 bars",
        "Retest of the iFVG box occurs within the 12-bar window",
        "Trade aligns with 200 EMA macro trend direction",
        "Stop loss includes dynamic ATR anti-hunt buffer"
      ],
      "pitfalls": [
        "Taking retests that take longer than 12 bars to arrive (loss of institutional momentum)",
        "Trading iFVGs that formed against the 200 EMA direction"
      ]
    },
