    "subTopics": [
      {
        "id": "sub-1",
        "title": "1. The Volume Weighted Average Price: The True Value Line of Dalal Street",
        "content": "\n          <p class=\"mb-3\">Unlike simple moving averages (SMAs) which treat low-volume holiday bars equal to massive option expiry blocks, VWAP weights every tick by exact trade volume:</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-tradeDark p-3 rounded-lg border border-tradeBorder font-mono text-xs text-accentGold my-2\">\n            VWAP = &sum;(Price &times; Volume) &divide; &sum;(Volume)\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"mb-3\">Above VWAP = Institutional Bullish Territory. Below VWAP = Institutional Bearish Territory.</p>\n        "
      },
      {
        "id": "sub-2",
        "title": "2. Standard Deviation Envelopes (±1σ, ±2σ): Overextended Mean Reversion Zones",
        "content": "\n          <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mb-4 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-gray-300\">\n            <li><strong>+1&sigma; and -1&sigma; Bands:</strong> 68.2% of all daily volume trades within this envelope. This is the normal value area.</li>\n            <li><strong>+2&sigma; and -2&sigma; Bands:</strong> 95.4% of all volume trades within 2 standard deviations. When price touches +2&sigma; on a range day, it is statistically overextended. Buying here is retail suicide; smart money fades this back to VWAP.</li>\n          </ul>\n        "
      },
      {
        "id": "sub-3",
        "title": "3. Anchored VWAP: Anchoring to Major RBI Announcements & Swing Lows",
        "content": "\n          <p class=\"mb-3\">Do not reset VWAP only at 9:15 AM each morning. Anchor your VWAP to major market structural events: the RBI Interest Rate decision candle, Union Budget day, or the swing low of the week.</p>\n        "
      }
    ],
