    "subTopics": [
      {
        "id": "sub-1",
        "title": "1. The Greek Anatomy: Delta, Gamma, Theta Decay & Implied Volatility",
        "content": "\n          <ul class=\"list-disc pl-5 mb-4 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-gray-300\">\n            <li><strong>Delta (&Delta;):</strong> The rate of change of option price per 1-point move in the underlying index.</li>\n            <li><strong>Gamma (&Gamma;):</strong> The acceleration of Delta. High gamma means delta changes violently with every tick.</li>\n            <li><strong>Theta (&Theta;):</strong> Time decay. The enemy of the buyer in the morning, but completely neutral on explosive 5-minute afternoon breakouts.</li>\n            <li><strong>Vega (&nu;):</strong> Sensitivity to Implied Volatility (IV).</li>\n          </ul>\n        "
      },
      {
        "id": "sub-2",
        "title": "2. The Hyper-Gamma Blast Phenomenon: Why Gamma Approaches Infinity Near Expiry",
        "content": "\n          <p class=\"mb-3\">In the Black-Scholes formula, Gamma is inversely proportional to $\\sqrt{T}$ where $T$ is time remaining:</p>\n          <div class=\"bg-tradeDark p-3 rounded-lg border border-tradeBorder font-mono text-xs text-accentGold my-2\">\n            &Gamma; &prop; 1 &divide; (S &times; &sigma; &times; &radic;T)\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"mb-3\">As expiry afternoon approaches ($T \\rightarrow 0$), gamma spikes exponentially. If price crosses into your strike, delta leaps from 0.15 to 0.70. A ₹20 option suddenly behaves like a ₹75 option, producing the legendary <strong>Hero-Zero 200% to 500% profit surge</strong>.</p>\n        "
      },
      {
        "id": "sub-3",
        "title": "3. The 1:15 PM Rule & The Sweet Spot Strike Selection Strategy",
        "content": "\n          <p class=\"mb-3\">Do not enter before 1:15 PM. Morning theta decay will eat 60% of your premium while you wait. Between 1:15 PM and 2:30 PM, market makers square off intraday short straddles. Look for strikes trading strictly in the <strong>₹15 to ₹35 sweet spot</strong> with expanding open interest unwinding.</p>\n        "
      }
    ],
